;; cloud-itonami-apex.agent-edge-writes.edn
;;
;; The write templates the agent ingress Worker carries, pinned here because the
;; Worker itself is not in this repository. `services/agent-edge` moved to
;; cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-apex, which owns agent.itonami.cloud; a byte copy
;; stayed behind here until 2026-09-09, carrying the same Worker name and the
;; same custom domain, so a deploy from this tree could overwrite the live one.
;;
;; `mobile/test/cloud/itonami/mobile/terminal_test.cljk` compares this table with
;; `cloud.itonami.mobile.terminal/offered-writes`. It used to slurp the Worker's
;; source through `../services/agent-edge/src/index.js`. A sibling path that
;; resolves on one machine and not on another is a check that reports a pass
;; wherever it cannot look, which is the defect ADR-2608136000 §2 names, so what
;; crosses the repository boundary is this artifact instead -- the seam
;; cloud-itonami-cli already uses for the tables this app generates.
;;
;; A pinned copy of a generated thing is the thing that drifts, so it is checked:
;; `scripts/verify-itonami-surface-split.cljs` in the superproject compares
;; :writes against the live Worker source, because the superproject is the only
;; checkout that holds both repositories. Refresh this file from the apex tree
;; and move :source/revision with it; do not edit :writes to make a test pass.
{:source/repo     "cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-apex"
 :source/path     "services/agent-edge/src/index.js"
 :source/revision "a3c578507b9a40ae3e3919021c18189d22db8ca4"
 :source/observed "2026-09-09"
 :writes ["/api/agent-bots/{id}/messages"
          "/p/{profile}/api/sessions"
          "/p/{profile}/api/sessions/{session}/messages"]}
